{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116222",
      "title": "Converting Signals To Observables",
      "lectureOrder": 214,
      "videoOrder": 205,
      "sourceHash": "c6da10794f9fd5dd5508ca62ec3e08d2ca6ffc747d9317f5ec7de49fca5b5edb",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "So, you cannot just choose whether you want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "use a signal or RxJS in a certain scenario,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 12.063,
          "en": "but you can also convert values between these two worlds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 17.22,
          "en": "For example, let's say we want to listen to that clickCount,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.22,
          "end": 21.87,
          "en": "not with help of that effect, but by converting this signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 23.64,
          "en": "to an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.64,
          "end": 27.24,
          "en": "You can do this, for example, here in the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.24,
          "end": 32.24,
          "en": "by calling Angular's toObservable function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 37.58,
          "en": "which must be imported from @angular/core/rxjs-interop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 48.27,
          "en": "And toObservable then does what its name implies;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 48.27,
          "end": 52.71,
          "en": "it takes a signal, the clickCount here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 52.71,
          "end": 55.71,
          "en": "and converts that to an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 55.71,
          "end": 59.52,
          "en": "And you should not execute this signal function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 64.52,
          "en": "but instead pass the un-executed signal to toObservable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 71.28,
          "en": "It's also worth noting that you must use toObservable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 71.28,
          "end": 75.36,
          "en": "in places where you could also inject values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 75.36,
          "end": 79.41,
          "en": "So, either in the constructor or here as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 79.41,
          "end": 81.48,
          "en": "for a property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 81.48,
          "end": 85.47,
          "en": "So, we could also add the clickCount observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 85.47,
          "end": 88.08,
          "en": "by adding this dollar sign at the end, which is a common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 88.08,
          "end": 91.47,
          "en": "notation for observable properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 94.83,
          "en": "that you add a dollar sign at the end to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 94.83,
          "end": 97.593,
          "en": "that it's an observable that's stored in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 99.27000000000001,
          "end": 103.02000000000001,
          "en": "And then you could also call toObservable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 103.02000000000001,
          "end": 106.95,
          "en": "to convert clickCount as an observable and store the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 106.95,
          "end": 109.02000000000001,
          "en": "in this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 109.02000000000001,
          "end": 113.67,
          "en": "And with that, we then have this clickCount observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 113.67,
          "end": 118.47,
          "en": "And instead of using an effect for listening to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 118.47,
          "end": 122.38,
          "en": "changes here, we could go to ngOnInit again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 123.33,
          "end": 127.02,
          "en": "and use this clickCount, the observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 127.02,
          "end": 128.943,
          "en": "and call subscribe again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 133.32,
          "en": "And then again, pass this observer object to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 133.32,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "set up the next function that will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 139.2,
          "en": "for every new value that's submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 139.2,
          "end": 142.07999999999998,
          "en": "And we would then get that value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 142.07999999999998,
          "end": 146.4,
          "en": "And TypeScript even correctly detects that it'll be a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 146.4,
          "end": 150.933,
          "en": "because our Signal is managing a number, starting with zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 153,
          "end": 155.31,
          "en": "And we can then, of course, also console.log here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 155.31,
          "end": 158.57999999999998,
          "en": "and copy this console.log statement and use that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 158.57999999999998,
          "end": 159.633,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 161.25,
          "end": 165.45,
          "en": "Well, and just as before, we also might want to copy this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 165.45,
          "end": 168.84,
          "en": "unsubscribe function here with onDestroy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 168.84,
          "end": 172.53,
          "en": "and store this subscription so that we can clean up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 172.53,
          "end": 175.38,
          "en": "this subscription if the surrounding component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 175.38,
          "end": 177.003,
          "en": "should ever get removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 179.57999999999998,
          "end": 183.15,
          "en": "But with that, we now did convert this signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 183.15,
          "end": 187.71,
          "en": "to an observable, or we created an extra observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 187.71,
          "end": 190.98,
          "en": "based on that signal, to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 190.98,
          "end": 194.07,
          "en": "And we can therefore still update that signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 194.07,
          "end": 196.47,
          "en": "That will still work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 196.47,
          "end": 200.82,
          "en": "But a new value will then be emitted in that observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 200.82,
          "end": 203.223,
          "en": "that was created with help of toObservable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 204.42000000000002,
          "end": 207.32999999999998,
          "en": "So that's also just another function that in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 207.32999999999998,
          "end": 208.953,
          "en": "produces an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 210.39,
          "end": 213.12,
          "en": "And now we're logging based on that observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 213.12,
          "end": 216.32999999999998,
          "en": "So if you save everything and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 216.32999999999998,
          "end": 218.57999999999998,
          "en": "you'll again see that with every click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 218.57999999999998,
          "end": 220.38,
          "en": "we got a new log message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 220.38,
          "end": 225.38,
          "en": "But now, by converting or by also listening to that signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 226.07999999999998,
          "end": 228.063,
          "en": "with help of an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
